{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791830807,"nonce":"Homdvv7ZOw+iyasoIjofJRhIC90=","message":"Decision (amended after review of PR 184): background work keeps the 2 s budget for multi-host walks (resolve, legacy re-resolve) but a click's plain re-verify (one host, at most two requests) gets its own 7 s budget, since the first request to a host after a console start needs a robots fetch plus a full rate interval (at least 3.75 s). The job page and the apply-button fragment start a re-verify of a stale live link in the background without waiting, so the next click finds it fresh. Automatic saves never overwrite a user-set link (WHERE on the ON CONFLICT update). At most 8 background jobs in flight; past that the stored link answers and nothing starts. A walk that finds no answer (a login-wall row that never settles) is not repeated for the group within 24 h, in memory in the console; this also covers the filed follow-up about re-walking on every look. Reason: review findings F2, N1, N2, N3, N6.","files":null}]}